    "title": "<p>Cancer patients who should be tested for constitutional (germline) disease-causing <em>TP53</em> variants<sup>a</sup> {32457520}</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "",
    "copyright": "Adapted from: Frebourg T, Bajalica Lagercrantz S, Oliveira C, et al. Guidelines for the Li-Fraumeni and heritable TP53-related cancer syndromes. Eur J Hum Genet. 2020 Oct;28(10):1379–86. PMID:32457520; https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; mso-yfti-tbllook: 1184; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 0; mso-yfti-firstrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid; height: 4.0pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 531.1pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 4.0pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Recommendation 1</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 1; page-break-inside: avoid; height: 85.45pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 531.1pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 85.45pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">All patients who meet the modified Chompret criteria should be tested for constitutional pathogenic <em>TP53</em> variants:</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><em><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Familial presentation:</span></em><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\"> proband with a <em>TP53</em> core tumour (breast cancer, soft tissue sarcoma, osteosarcoma, CNS tumour, adrenocortical carcinoma) before the age of 46&nbsp;years AND at least one first-degree or second-degree relative with a core tumour before the age of 56&nbsp;years; <em>or</em></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><em><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Multiple primitive tumours:</span></em><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\"> proband with multiple tumours, including two <em>TP53</em> core tumours, the first of which occurred before the age of 46&nbsp;years, irrespective of family history; <em>or</em></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><em><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Rare tumours:</span></em><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\"> patient with adrenocortical carcinoma, choroid plexus carcinoma, or rhabdomyosarcoma of embryonal anaplastic subtype, irrespective of family history; <em>or</em></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><em><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Very early onset breast cancer:</span></em><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\"> breast cancer before the age of 31&nbsp;years, irrespective of family history</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 2; page-break-inside: avoid; height: 4.0pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 531.1pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 4.0pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Recommendation 2</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 3; page-break-inside: avoid; height: 4.0pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 531.1pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 4.0pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Children and adolescents should be tested for constitutional pathogenic <em>TP53</em> variants if presenting with:</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Hypodiploid acute lymphoblastic leukaemia; <em>or</em></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Otherwise unexplained <em>SHH</em>-driven medulloblastoma; <em>or</em></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold; mso-bidi-font-style: italic;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Jaw osteosarcoma</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 4; page-break-inside: avoid; height: 4.0pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 531.1pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 4.0pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Recommendation 3</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 5; page-break-inside: avoid; height: 4.0pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 531.1pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 4.0pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Patients who develop a second primary tumour within the radiotherapy field of a first core <em>TP53</em> tumour that occurred before the age of 46&nbsp;years should be tested for constitutional pathogenic <em>TP53</em> variants.</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 6; page-break-inside: avoid; height: 4.0pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 531.1pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 4.0pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Recommendation 4</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 7; page-break-inside: avoid; height: 4.0pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 531.1pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 4.0pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin-left: 12.25pt; text-indent: -12.25pt; mso-list: l1 level1 lfo2; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">a.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Patients older than 46&nbsp;years presenting with breast cancer without personal or familial history fulfilling the Chompret criteria should not be tested for constitutional pathogenic <em>TP53</em> variants.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"margin-left: 12.25pt; text-indent: -12.25pt; mso-list: l1 level1 lfo2; tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">b.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp; </span></span></span><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Any patient presenting with isolated breast cancer and not fulfilling the Chompret criteria, in whom a disease-causing <em>TP53</em> variant has been identified, should be referred to an expert multidisciplinary team for discussion.</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 8; page-break-inside: avoid; height: 4.0pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 531.1pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 4.0pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Recommendation 5</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 9; mso-yfti-lastrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid; height: 4.0pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 531.1pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 4.0pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"708\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Children with any cancer from southern and south-eastern Brazilian families should be tested for the p.R337H Brazilian founder constitutional pathogenic <em>TP53</em> variant.</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><sup><span style=\"mso-no-proof: yes;\">a</span></sup><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-no-proof: yes;\">Testing</span><span style=\"mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman';\"> for disease-causing <em>TP53</em> variants should be performed before starting treatment in order to avoid in variant carriers, if possible, radiotherapy and genotoxic chemotherapy and to prioritize surgical treatments.</span></p>",
